                <pb facs="0314" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5823/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-17T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>71. Your 138, June 10, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>This Government will agree to suggestion of Swedish Government that Articles 11
                    and 12 of the Consular Convention of 1910, be eliminated in their entirety.
                    Referring draft of note to Foreign Office suggested in Department instruction
                    No. 644 of April 22, 1920, make necessary changes therein to effect entire
                    elimination of said articles and proceed in accordance with that
                    instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
